<text top="931" left="77" width="528" height="27" font="4"><i><b>Ministry of Defence Current Situation Reports </b></i></text>
<text top="983" left="77" width="40" height="19" font="0"><i><b>9.233</b></i></text>
<text top="987" left="116" width="8" height="15" font="5"> �</text>
<text top="984" left="153" width="591" height="19" font="6"><i>In the aftermath of the weekend marches, Anthony Stephens, the head of DS10,  </i></text>
<text top="1011" left="153" width="321" height="19" font="6"><i>circulated the 61st Current Situation Report.</i></text>
<text top="1010" left="474" width="6" height="12" font="7"><i>1</i></text>
<text top="1011" left="480" width="319" height="19" font="6"><i> Anthony Stephens told this Inquiry that the  </i></text>
<text top="1038" left="153" width="658" height="19" font="6"><i>documents in this series were intended to draw together information from various sources  </i></text>
<text top="1064" left="153" width="279" height="19" font="6"><i>to provide ministers and officials with “</i></text>
<text top="1065" left="432" width="365" height="19" font="12"><i>a fleeting picture of what had occurred in the past </i></text>
</page>
