<text top="21" left="541" width="275" height="15" font="13"><i> Chapter 9: The weeks before Bloody Sunday</i></text>
<text top="147" left="162" width="64" height="19" font="12"><i>24 hours</i></text>
<text top="147" left="226" width="10" height="19" font="6"><i>”,</i></text>
<text top="146" left="236" width="6" height="12" font="7"><i>2</i></text>
<text top="147" left="242" width="520" height="19" font="6"><i> and if possible to give an indication of situations that might arise in the </i></text>
<text top="174" left="162" width="127" height="19" font="6"><i>immediate future.</i></text>
<text top="173" left="289" width="6" height="12" font="7"><i>3</i></text>
<text top="174" left="295" width="491" height="19" font="6"><i> In the week before Bloody Sunday a Current Situation Report was </i></text>
<text top="201" left="162" width="229" height="19" font="6"><i>produced on each working day.</i></text>
<text top="200" left="391" width="6" height="12" font="7"><i>4</i></text>
<text top="233" left="162" width="8" height="10" font="8"><i>1 </i></text>
<text top="232" left="174" width="75" height="14" font="9"><a href="..\evidence\G\G70B.PDF#page=1"><i>G70B.441.3-5</i></a></text>
<text top="252" left="162" width="8" height="10" font="8"><i>2 </i></text>
<text top="252" left="174" width="68" height="14" font="9"><a href="..\transcripts\Archive\Ts273.htm#p109"><i>Day 273/109</i></a></text>
<text top="271" left="162" width="8" height="10" font="8"><i>3 </i></text>
